{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::execute` receives a context for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node` and computes its\ncompleted answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::future::Future;\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Select inputs through cx and compute the completed answer.\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        cx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nAn `Ok` value is the answer defined by\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.answer`.\nAn `Err` value reports a [validation error](running-criteria.md#habeas-req-requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ValidationError).",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged this from the supplied test sources only. I did not request any implementation source.\n\n**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.execute`:**\n1. `Criterion::execute` receives a context for the criterion's source node.\n2. It computes the completed answer, and an `Ok` value is that answer. This includes a negative assessment, per the cited `criterion_trait.answer`.\n3. An `Err` value reports a `ValidationError`.\n4. The future is `Send`, as the trait signature shows.\n\n**Coverage:**\n- **Context for the source node, and computing the answer.**\n  - `agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` runs `verify` on `Review(Node(1))`. It asserts the computed output, `result` false and the rationale. It also asserts that the recorded dependency is `Node(1)` with the node's content fingerprint, so the context really is bound to the source node.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` runs the agent-based execution through the context. It asserts `value.output().result` and the stored dependency on node 1. It also asserts the intermediate request text.\n  - `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` checks that the `Ok` output holds the agent's determination and rationale and that the stored record equals the answer.\n- **`Ok` is the completed answer, including a negative one.**\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]` shows that `false` is returned as `Ok`. It asserts the output is false, the dependencies are correct, and the stored output is `json!(false)`.\n  - The SDK test above covers a negative judgment, `determination` false, that is persisted and reused.\n- **`Err` reports a validation error.**\n  - `NoAgentConfigured` is asserted in the runner test, and nothing is stored.\n  - `Graph(\"load\")`, `Graph(\"store\")` and `Graph(\"missing\")`, the last raised from a callback, are asserted in `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments`.\n  - `Agent(_)` for an invalid typed submission is asserted in `invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error`.\n  - `Output(error)` from a decode failure is asserted in the decode-errors test.\n  - The `Agent` string payload and the `Graph` source are asserted in `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload`.\n  - These tests also assert that failed executions store no evidence, which fits the `Err` versus completed `Ok` distinction.\n- **`Send` future.** `contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` runs `verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `refresh_evidence` through a `send()` helper. That enforces the `Send` bound at compile time, and it asserts the answer values (17, 23).\n\nI found no scenario in the requirement that lacks a test with a matching assertion. Every test has a `{test}` reference to the subject. The cited `criterion_trait` and `criterion_trait.answer` are context only.",
